ame limit shapes for the\nIDLA or rotor-router cluster, respectively.\nThe more delicate question concerns the abelian sandpile model. For tree nested\nfractal graphs, this can be addressed using results from [46]. For non-tree nested\nfractal graphs, the problem appears to be open to the best of our knowledge. (See\nalso [22] for numerical results of the sandpile model on various gasket-type fractal\ngraphs.)\nExplosions in sandpile growth.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOverpartitions in terms of 2-adic valuation (https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00010-024-01117-6)\nciteturn2search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.2 years ago; Crawled: last month;   * Mircea Merca^{1,2} ... This formula implies a certain type of partitions with restrictions for which we provide two Ramanujan-type congruences and present as open problems two infinite families of linear inequalities.\n\n# Overpartitions in terms of 2-adic valuation\n\n  * Open access\n  * Published: 06 September 2024\n\n  * Volume 99, pages 1153–1173 (2025)\n  * Cite this article\n\nYou have full access to this open access article\n\nDownload PDF\n\nSave article\n\nView saved research\n\nAequationes mathematicae Aims and scope Submit manuscript\n\nOverpartitions in terms of 2-adic valuation\n\nDownload PDF\n\n  * Mircea Merca^{1,2} \n\n  * 2519 Accesses\n\n  * 6 Citations\n\n  * Explore all metrics\n\n## Abstract\n\nIn this paper, we consider the 2-adic valuation of integers and provide an alternative representation for the generating function of the number of overpartitions of an integer. As a consequence of this result, we obtain a new formula and a new combinatorial interpretation for the number of overpartitions of an integer. This formula implies a certain type of partitions with restrictions for which we provide two Ramanujan-type congruences and present as open problems two infinite families of linear inequalities. ----------------------------------