ing to have a combinatorial interpretation of Theorems 1.1\n\nand 1.2. More importantly, it would be very interesting to ﬁnd q-series identities like (1.2)\n\nfor Theorems 2.1 and 2.7, for which one can provide direct proofs.\n\nIn their study on averaged truncations of Jacobi’s triple product identity, Andrews and\n\nMerca [2, Question (2)] and Guo and Zeng [8, Conjecture 6.1] posed the following conjecture:\n\nConjecture 1. For positive integers m, k, R, S with 1≤S<R2, the coeﬃcient of q m in\n\n(−1)k−1\n\n(q S, q R−S, q R;q R)∞\n\n0≤n<k(−1)n qn+1\n\n2R−nS (1−q(2 n+1)S)\n\nis non-negative.\n\n14\n\nIn 2015, Mao [11] and Yee [25] independently proved Conjecture 1 by diﬀerent means;\n\nMao’s proof is algebraic, while Yee’s proof is combinatorial. The conjecture was later also\n\nconﬁrmed by He, Ji, and Zang [9] using combinatorial arguments. More recently, Wang and\n\nYee [19, Theorem 2.3], as well as Schlosser and the author [18, Theorem 1.1], conﬁrmed Con-\n\njecture 1 by establishing diﬀerent q-series identities. More results on averaged truncations\n\nof theta series can be found in the papers by Wang and Yee [20], by Xia, Yee and Zhao [22],\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nProofs of some conjectures of Merca on truncated series involving the Rogers-Ramanujan functions (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/388596083_Proofs_of_some_conjectures_of_Merca_on_truncated_series_involving_the_Rogers-Ramanujan_functions)\nciteturn2search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 months ago; # Proofs of some conjectures of Merca on truncated series involving the Rogers-Ramanujan functions ... Recently, Merca investigated two partition functions whose generating functions are the Göllnitz–Gordon functions. ... In this paper, we reprove this ex-conjecture by providing an explicit series form with nonnegative coefficients, which is reminiscent of the results of Andrews-Merca and Guo-Zeng.\n\nArticle\n\n# Proofs of some conjectures of Merca on truncated series involving the Rogers-Ramanujan functions\n\n  * February 2025\n  * Journal of Combinatorial Theory Series A 210:105956\n\nDOI:10.1016/j.jcta.2024.105956\n\nAuthors:\n\nYongqiang Chen\n\nYongqiang Chen\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nOlivia X.M. Yao\n\nOlivia X.M. Yao\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nRequest full-text PDF\n\nTo read the full-text of this research, you can request a copy directly from the authors.\n\nImage: ResearchGate Logo\n\nDiscover the world's research\n\n  * 25+ million members\n  * 160+ million publication pages\n  * 2.3+ billion citations\nJoin for free\n\n## No full-text available\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nTo read the full-text of this research,\nyou can request a copy directly from the authors.\n\nRequest full-text PDF\n\n## Citations (12)\n\n## References (26)\n\n... (1, 2, 3), (1,2,5), (1,2,7), (1,3,4), (1,3,5). ...\n\n... (1, 2, 3), (1,2,5), (1,2,7), (1,3,4), (1,3,5). ...\n\n... Remark The triples (1,3,8), (1,4,5) and (1,4,7) were not listed by Zhou [13]. Table 4 The case A = 5/2 and B = 3/2 ...\n\nA general positivity result on coefficients of certain q-series\n\nArticle\n\nFull-text available\n\n  * Oct 2025\n  * J ALGEBR COMB\n\n  * Ji-Cai Liu\n  * RAMANUJAN J\n\n  * Jing Jin\n  * Eric H. Liu\n  * Ernest X. W. Xia\n\nRecently, Mao established two truncated sums of theta series and presented their partition-theoretic interpretations. In this paper, we provide new partition-theoretic interpretations for the two truncated sums of theta series given by Mao based on the minimal excludant in congruence classes.\n\nView\n\nShow abstract\n\n... In recent years, linear inequalities involving various partition functions have been investigated by Andrews and Merca [2][3][4], Ballantine and Feigon [5], Ballantine and Merca [6], Chan et al. [10], Chen and Yao [11], Chern and Xia [12], Ding and Sun [15], Guo and Zeng [16], Mao [18], Merca [19][20][21][22], Merca et al. [24], Wang and Yee [26], Xia [27], Xia et al. [28], Yao [31][32][33][34], and Zhou [35]. ...\n\n... The proof of Lemma 2.2 is similar to that of (2.1) in [11]. Here we omit the details. ...\n\nProof of a conjecture of Merca on the cubic partition function\n\nArticle\n\nFull-text available\n\n  * Apr 2025\n  * RAMANUJAN J\n\n  * Jingzhao Zhang\n  * Olivia X. M. Yao\n\nA cubic partition is an integer partition wherein the even parts can appear in two colors. Recently, Merca investigated the partition function A(n) which counts the difference between the number of cubic partitions of n into an even number of parts and the number of cubic partitions of n into an odd number of parts. At the end of his paper, he posed a conjecture on linear inequalities involving A(n). In this paper, we confirm Merca’s conjecture by using some results on truncated sums.\n\nView\n\nShow abstract\n\n... Motivated by Andrews and Merca's work, a number of identities involving truncated sums of certain classical identities have been proved, since one can find some papers on the subject by Andrews and Merca [3], Bachraoui [4], Ballantine and Feigon [5], Ballantine and Merca [6,7], Ballantine, Merca, Passary and Yee [8], Chan, Ho and Mao [9], Chen and Yao [10], Chern [11], Chern and Xia [12], Guo and Zeng [13], Mao [14], Merca [15][16][17][18], Merca, Wang and Yee [19], Wang and Yee [20], Xia, Yee and Zhao [21], Xia and Zhao [22], Yao and Zhang [23][24][25][26], and Yee [27]. As corollaries of those truncated versions of theta series, many infinite families of linear inequalities involving certain partition functions, such as overpartitions and partitions with odd parts distinct, have been proved. ...\n\nMotivated by their work, linear inequalities involving various partition functions have been established in recent years. Recently, Merca investigated two partition functions whose generating functions are the Göllnitz–Gordon functions. He also posed a conjecture on linear inequalities for the coefficients of the Göllnitz–Gordon functions. In this paper, we confirm Merca’s conjecture based on a classical result owing to Pólya and Szegö.\n\nView\n\nShow abstract\n\nSome conjectures of Ballantine and Merca on truncated sums and the minimal excludant in congruences classes\n\nArticle\n\n  * Feb 2025\n\n  * Olivia X. M. Yao\n\nView\n\nTruncated Hecke–Rogers type series—part II\n\nArticle\n\nFull-text available\n\n  * Jun 2021\n  * RAMANUJAN J\n\n  * Chun Wang\n  * Ae Ja Yee\n\nMotivated by the works on truncated theta series of Andrews–Merca and Guo–Zeng, the authors of this paper investigated some Hecke–Rogers type double series in their earlier paper. As a continuation of their study, in this paper, a further investigation on double series will be presented.\n\nView\n\nShow abstract\n\nTruncated Jacobi triple product series\n\nArticle\n\n  * Aug 2019\n  * J COMB THEORY A\n\n  * Chun Wang\n  * Ae Ja Yee\n\nIn their study of truncated theta series, Andrews-Merca and Guo-Zeng made a conjecture on Jacobi's triple product identity, which is settled by Mao and Yee independently. In this paper, we reprove this ex-conjecture by providing an explicit series form with nonnegative coefficients, which is reminiscent of the results of Andrews-Merca and Guo-Zeng. We also provide a companion theorem to this ex-conjecture.\n\nView\n\nShow abstract\n\nTruncated Theta Series and Rogers-Ramanujan Functions\n\nArticle\n\n  * Sep 2021\n\n  * Mircea Merca\n\nWe consider the squares of the Rogers-Ramanujan functions and for each $S\\in\\{1,2\\}$ we obtain a linear recurrence relation for the number of partitions of n into parts congruent to $\\pm S\\bmod{5}$. In this context, we conjecture that for $1\\leqslant S < R$, $k\\geqslant 1$, the theta series $\\frac{(-1)^k}{(q^S,q^{R-S};q^R)_\\infty} \\sum_{j=k}^{\\infty} (-1)^j q^{j(j+1)R/2-jS}\\big(1-q^{(2j+1)S}\\big)$ has nonnegative coefficients. This improves a conjecture given by G. E. Andrews and M. Merca in 2012, which was proved independently three years later by A. J. Yee using combinatorial methods and R. Mao via partial theta functions. Combinatorial interpretations of this new conjecture give for each $S \\in\\{1,2,3,4\\}$ an infinite family of linear homogeneous inequalities for the number of partitions of n into parts congruent to $\\pm S\\bmod{5}$. Twenty identities involving Rogers-Ramanujan functions are experimentally discovered considering Jacobi's triple product identity and Watson's quintuple product identity.\n\nView--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSearch (https://www.cambridge.org/core/search?filters%5Bkeywords%5D=PARTITIONS)\nciteturn2search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; These include a Franklin-type involution proving a parametrized identity that generalizes Andrews’ bivariate generating function, and two families of Andrews–Beck type congruences. ...   * ### A CONJECTURE OF MERCA ON CONGRUENCES MODULO POWERS OF 2 FOR PARTITIONS INTO DISTINCT PARTS ... Merca [‘Ramanujan-type congruences modulo 4 for partitions into distinct parts’, An.\n\n  * Part of\n    * Additive number theory; partitions\n    * Combinatorics\n  * JULIA Q. D. DU, DAZHAO TANG\n  * Journal:\n    Bulletin of the Australian Mathematical Society / Volume 109 / Issue 1 / February 2024\nPublished online by Cambridge University Press:\n    27 March 2023, pp. 26-36\nPrint publication:\n    February 2024\n  *     * Article\n    *       * Get access\n\nCheck if you have access via personal or institutional login\n\nLog in Register\n\n      *     * Export citation\n  * View abstract\n\nLet Image$Q(n)$ denote the number of partitions of n into distinct parts. Merca [‘Ramanujan-type congruences modulo 4 for partitions into distinct parts’, An. Şt. Univ. Ovidius Constanţa 30(3) (2022), 185–199] derived some congruences modulo Image$4$ and Image$8$ for Image$Q(